Subject: [PATCH 09/15] fix-phone-sizes: M-48, a card's "N places" / "2 levels"
 line is 12 px (was 11.5), on one line

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
---
 public/styles.css | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/public/styles.css b/public/styles.css
index d285511..d2e958d 100644
--- a/public/styles.css
+++ b/public/styles.css
@@ -1645,6 +1645,9 @@ html[data-mode="map"] .tagline, html[data-mode="insights"] .tagline { display: n
   body.is-previewing .results { --sheet-peek: 156px; }
 }
 
+/* M-48: the card's "5 places" / "2 levels" line keeps to the 12 px floor, on one line. */
+.sal-sub { font-size: 12px; white-space: nowrap; }
+
 /* M-40 meets fix-data-3's longer names ("Non-Technical Project, Program and Product Management": its end was cut by
    0.42 px at 360 px, and more on narrower phones): a split name that fits whole in two lines flows as one text
    (app.js fitCheckLabels); on the narrowest phones in 13 px, then 12 px, with tighter gaps in its row. */
